WEBVTT

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:48.320
How much long is this going to go on?

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.540
I don't know how to do anything else.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.470
Then you'd better learn. And you'd better make some money somehow.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.530
I will. I will.

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:59.050
When? That's what I want to know. When?

00:01:59.230 --> 00:01:59.970
You'll see. I'll...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.160
We'll find a way, maybe today.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.650
I don't know.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:17.250
Mr. Kirby?

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:18.530
Oh, hello, Bob. My wife here?

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:20.470
Yes, over there with your little blonde.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:27.250
Hello, darling.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:29.980
Sorry I'm late.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.400
Oh, not my business, will you, dear?

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.460
I didn't take a job suddenly, if that's what you mean.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.220
I'm much too old for that sort of thing.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:39.720
Now, as a matter of fact, I waited for somebody who didn't come.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.080
Hello, Edna. Where'd you two meet up this afternoon?

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.990
Oh, I called her and invited her.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:47.320
You don't mind, do you, dear?

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.780
I've always known each other for years now.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.560
In fact, I'll become a friend of the family if I'm not careful.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.280
There, you've gotten her to talk.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:55.740
Oh, that's wonderful.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:58.680
She sat absorbed in that paper ever since she got here.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:02:59.970
You want to know what's happening in the world?

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.460
What is happening in the world, Edna?

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.430
Well, here's a man robbed a woman.

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:06.950
Got 22 francs.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:08.540
Happens every day.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.220
Yes, but he murdered her, too.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.200
That's a poor return on his investment.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:14.600
Well, when they let him go, send him around to me.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.320
They'll get rid of my aunt the same way.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:17.440
I'll give him a million francs.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:20.620
Oh, Bill, don't say your aunt said no again.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.120
Yes, and very friendly.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:25.520
Have they told you about Mrs. Henderson?

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:26.300
Mm-hmm.

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:27.560
I took the liberty, sir.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:28.860
Oh, thank you.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.070
And a martini sec for you.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:32.640
Thanks.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.220
Everything all right otherwise?

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.580
What's Mrs. Henderson going to do with all her money?

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:39.980
Well, she's going to give it to me.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:41.850
Then why worry?

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.910
Because she lived to be a hundred and that's too long.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.520
I'll get rid of her for you.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:46.740
For a million francs?

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:48.910
Just for love.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:03:59.620
No.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:05.170
Bill, why don't you tell her now, this minute?

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:07.830
Yes, tell me, darling.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.960
Don't you think this is a rather odd place to discuss a personal matter?

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.800
You don't have to shout it out.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.790
Just say it soft and distinctly.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.600
Helen, Edna and I...

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.310
Edna and you think you love each other, is that it?

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:25.890
Yes, I'm afraid that's it.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.960
And, um, would you like me to step out a little bit?

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:34.930
Not at all, darling. You stay where you are, we'll step out.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:35.990
How thoughtful.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:38.680
I didn't want it to happen this way.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.460
But anything you like, Bill, as long as you pay.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:42.480
Meaning what?

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.960
Meaning she'll let you go if you give her money.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:47.910
I mean that and a good deal more, my pet.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.630
We live entirely on credit, Bill and I.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.180
Well, you must have guessed it by now.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:56.240
You must have guessed how the credit and everything else revolves around that aunt of his dying.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:59.980
And if she takes too long, well, you'll get tired of...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.750
waiting, Edna, and old Bill.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.680
Well, I'll get along now.

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:08.010
I guess you two got quite a bit to think about.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:11.360
Oh, yes, and in the meantime, Edna,

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.080
you better just go along being a friend

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:18.080
of the family, huh? Bye. Bye.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.540
You know, Helen took it nicely, didn't she?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.280
Nicely, about demanding a fortune you haven't got.

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:34.380
I'll get it somehow.

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:36.860
I love you, Bill, I really do.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.770
But Helen was right about one thing.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.570
If you don't do something soon, I can't wait.

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:43.110
You understand that, don't you?

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:44.640
I understand only one thing.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:46.320
I can't lose you and I won't lose you.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:47.880
Did you drop this, sir?

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:52.440
I don't think so.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:17.580
i guess i did you want another drink no thanks mind if i go no if you must you must yourself

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:37.410
want to see if I can throw two aces. And if you do? The answer will be yes. Yes to what? Nothing

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:42.300
important, just an idea. Goodbye darling. Bye.

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:35.520
Robbery has to get you worse.

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:36.900
Look what you've done.

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:37.640
I didn't do it.

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:39.400
You think the police will believe that?

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:41.500
I'm going to kill her.

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:47.580
I'll get you out of this.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:59.110
I don't know what else.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:01.400
I'm your only hope.

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:02.510
Did you hire that knife grinder?

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:05.420
Police might think so.

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:07.470
They could make it awkward for us.

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:09.330
Oh, Bill, don't be so serious.

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:11.090
I know just luck.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.700
And now you're rich and you can pay Helen off

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.790
and you and I can, what'll we do first?

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:18.900
It's not as easy as that, darling.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.760
You see, as the will and I suppose

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:23.580
a decent period of mourning

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.820
and Helen, of course, she has certain ideas.

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:27.870
We'll have to be careful for a while.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:29.210
How long?

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:30.950
Just be patient, darling.

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:33.340
Look, you've got to meet Helen now.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:34.520
Helen, always Helen.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:35.100
I'd like to...

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:35.900
It won't be long, darling.

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:34.200
Mrs. Kirby, back to Maygrave Police this year.

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:37.710
Mr. Kirby, are you your aunt?

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:39.660
Yes, I am.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:43.740
Do you happen to know of anyone who might have wanted to kill your aunt?

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:44.820
No one, no.

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:49.110
We've been told. It was the work of a burglar.

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:51.950
It was the work of a burglar, Mrs. Kirby, who took nothing.

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:05.370
Look where you're going.

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:06.150
What's the matter?

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:08.320
Nothing, nothing except you.

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:10.030
Here, let me have it.

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:15.250
I'm going to do such big things.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:17.990
Now you can't even afford to buy yourself a new pair of glasses.

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:18.810
I'll get some.

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:19.230
What?

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:19.650
Where?

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:21.370
Oh, I'm wasting my...

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:23.280
Why do you keep looking behind you all the time?

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.140
You can't see anything.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:25.310
I was thinking.

00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:28.430
You know, I still don't know how you lost your glasses.

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:29.890
I told you I fell down.

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:33.270
Where did you fall down?

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:33.850
In the street.

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:34.330
What street?

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:35.050
I don't know.

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:36.270
Oh, you don't know anything!

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:04.980
Who are you?

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:06.090
I'm the police.

00:14:06.390 --> 00:14:06.710
Police?

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:09.000
Your name is Joseph Hutter.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:13.390
I arrest you for the murder of Juliet Henderson and Elsie Cardew.

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:14.560
I didn't do it.

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:15.560
You come along with me.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:15.880
Now?

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:16.740
Yes, right now.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:17.720
What'll I say to her?

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:18.420
You come along.

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:19.840
You gotta help me, I can't see.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:21.540
Yes, I know, I found your glasses.

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:23.300
Now where are you going?

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:24.440
I'm going with this man.

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:26.030
With him, why?

00:14:26.270 --> 00:14:27.290
I found his glasses.

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:28.630
All my glasses.

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:29.690
You be careful.

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:34.540
Take him to headquarters.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:57.930
It's your way back from St. Clos without a pair of these.

00:14:58.610 --> 00:14:59.730
I didn't kill anybody.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.560
Who gave you Mrs. Henderson's dress?

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:03.020
I didn't kill anybody.

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:05.080
Why won't you speak out?

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:06.480
I've told you everything.

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.560
You told me that you broke into the house to what, Mrs. Henderson.

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:11.910
When you got there, you found her lying in a pool of blood.

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:13.790
And that somebody stepped on your glasses?

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:15.170
I didn't see who it was.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:18.760
How did you find your way back from St. Clu without your glasses?

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:26.320
You'll know what'll happen to you, don't you?

00:15:34.150 --> 00:15:37.380
I'm sorry if my nagging got you into this trouble.

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:39.240
That didn't have anything to do with it.

00:15:39.340 --> 00:15:40.840
Didn't it make you try to steal?

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:42.910
Well, maybe, but that's all it did.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:45.020
You didn't kill her, did you?

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:45.340
No.

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:47.270
And who did kill her?

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:49.000
I didn't see who it was.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:52.280
But I know there must have been someone with you, someone that helped you home.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:53.420
Who was it?

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:56.510
I can't tell.

00:16:00.092 --> 00:16:01.192
It was you that did it.

00:16:02.108 --> 00:16:02.568
You will.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:12.560
I'll see you tomorrow, Mr. Carmelio.

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:15.940
And remember, I take no responsibility for this.

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:19.770
Your career's at stake. And a man's head.

00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:44.240
Yeah, here we go.

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:44.770
Right.

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:51.220
Don't send me up some blood.

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:31.960
Thank you.

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:08.980
Paper, paper, get your afternoon paper, paper.

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:09.680
Give me them all.

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:13.880
Latest edition, paper, paper, get your afternoon paper.

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:15.480
Latest edition.

00:22:17.460 --> 00:22:18.500
He's still sleepy.

00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:40.320
Here they are. What did the morning papers say about the escape?

00:22:40.520 --> 00:22:41.800
Only that he got away.

00:22:46.780 --> 00:22:50.760
Jean-Pierre, are you sure he didn't try to leave a note anywhere?

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:52.800
Positive. We never took our eyes off him.

00:22:52.950 --> 00:22:54.710
Didn't he seem to be looking for someone?

00:22:54.830 --> 00:22:56.010
If he was, he didn't find him.

00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:57.440
What about the...

00:22:57.850 --> 00:22:58.050
What?

00:23:00.120 --> 00:23:06.700
Not a letter printed in the sea flame.

00:23:08.350 --> 00:23:10.930
A semi-official announcement was made in this morning's papers

00:23:10.930 --> 00:23:12.310
to the effect that Joseph Hurtown,

00:23:12.330 --> 00:23:14.210
awaiting trial for murder by the same assizes,

00:23:14.980 --> 00:23:17.020
has escaped from prison under inexplicable settings.

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:20.580
We are in a position to date.

00:23:22.520 --> 00:23:25.180
Joseph Hurtown did not escape. He was made to escape.

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:26.800
We are not in a position to give the details

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:28.780
of the odious comedy that was played last night.

00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:29.980
We are able to...

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:33.980
state that it was the police themselves who presided over this pseudo-escape.

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:36.200
What did anyone know about it?

00:23:36.400 --> 00:23:36.880
Not in here.

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:37.540
Not in here.

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:38.240
Nothing here.

00:23:39.050 --> 00:23:42.000
Look, run down to the offices of the Seaflair.

00:23:42.140 --> 00:23:42.980
I want the original.

00:24:29.280 --> 00:24:29.970
if he

00:24:30.160 --> 00:24:39.020
Excuse me, that's my paper.

00:26:56.590 --> 00:26:58.830
It had to happen. I'm sorry the whole thing happened.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:05.730
Paris is screaming for investigation. I've had 30 phone calls since I came in. Think I haven't got superiors too?

00:27:06.110 --> 00:27:12.260
What are they getting? Phone calls. If I don't lay my hands on the murderer, in 10 days I'll hand in my resignation.

00:27:12.840 --> 00:27:17.120
I'm afraid I'd have to accept it. Of course. In other words, if you don't lay hands on Joseph Ertan...

00:27:17.120 --> 00:27:22.630
Lay hands on the murderer. All right. Let's leave it at that. If there hadn't been a leak somewhere, I'd say take your time.

00:27:23.170 --> 00:27:29.090
But this situation is driving me out of my mind. Well, when you find something, let me know. That may be sooner than you...

00:27:31.490 --> 00:27:33.610
You get it.

00:27:33.960 --> 00:27:40.820
The editor was too bad that's been handled by so many people.

00:27:40.900 --> 00:27:42.140
There's no sense in looking for fingerprints.

00:27:42.340 --> 00:27:42.480
No.

00:27:42.960 --> 00:27:43.640
What does it tell you?

00:27:45.240 --> 00:27:45.420
You.

00:27:45.580 --> 00:27:47.170
I did it half the night.

00:27:48.300 --> 00:27:49.660
Paper comes from the Deux Magots.

00:27:50.060 --> 00:27:50.740
Saint-Germain-Dupuis.

00:27:50.840 --> 00:27:51.400
Do you know the place?

00:27:52.390 --> 00:27:53.130
I know the place.

00:27:53.490 --> 00:27:54.930
The writing was done with a left hand.

00:27:55.190 --> 00:27:58.330
Not by a left-handed person, but by somebody who knows that all left-handed writing looks

00:27:58.330 --> 00:27:59.110
pretty much alike.

00:28:00.820 --> 00:28:01.220
Intellectual.

00:28:01.880 --> 00:28:02.320
What was that?

00:28:02.780 --> 00:28:03.180
Intellectual.

00:28:03.420 --> 00:28:05.840
The kind that speaks and writes seven different languages, you know?

00:28:07.460 --> 00:28:11.140
If I'm going to give you a portrait of him, it's not strictly scientific.

00:28:11.540 --> 00:28:12.220
You go on.

00:28:12.760 --> 00:28:15.900
Well, unless I'm mistaken, we're dealing with an extraordinary individual.

00:28:16.700 --> 00:28:16.980
Train.

00:28:17.900 --> 00:28:26.310
I find here a curious mixture of willpower and weakness, of coldness and emotional capacity.

00:28:28.020 --> 00:28:28.640
Man's writing.

00:28:28.780 --> 00:28:29.880
Oh, yes, but...

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:32.750
I find traits here that are definitely feminine.

00:28:33.660 --> 00:28:37.140
Of course, I know this wouldn't be very convincing to an examining magistrate,

00:28:37.340 --> 00:28:42.040
but just to say, I could have told you much more had he written with his right hand.

00:28:42.940 --> 00:28:44.960
Now, there are stains on that paper,

00:28:45.080 --> 00:28:46.780
though, of course, they might have covered on the line of type art.

00:28:47.460 --> 00:28:50.800
But there, that is copy.

00:28:52.020 --> 00:28:56.010
Words that says it was written yesterday morning in the bar of the Derr

00:28:56.010 --> 00:28:59.520
may go by a polyglot customer who's probably drinking coffee.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:01.460
Colby has just committed a very right act.

00:29:01.560 --> 00:29:03.820
That's right. It's not exactly the sort I expected.

00:29:03.920 --> 00:29:05.200
Oh, you think it's her task accomplice?

00:29:06.060 --> 00:29:06.460
Colby.

00:29:07.220 --> 00:29:16.320
I never would read it. It would tell me far too much about her.

00:29:19.710 --> 00:29:21.310
Besides, I never have received one anyway.

00:30:32.760 --> 00:30:36.620
I'm glad to see you've stopped mourning.

00:30:37.780 --> 00:30:38.920
Oh, I'm still pretty sad.

00:30:39.640 --> 00:30:42.160
Looks like I'll be losing my man as soon as the will is probated.

00:30:42.670 --> 00:30:44.610
I weep for you, the walrus says.

00:30:45.240 --> 00:30:46.900
I deeply sympathize.

00:30:47.280 --> 00:30:49.870
With sighs and tears, she's stretched out both her eyes.

00:30:50.560 --> 00:30:51.700
What's the matter, Bill?

00:30:53.960 --> 00:30:57.770
Victor, do you drop in here often?

00:30:58.310 --> 00:30:59.330
I-I smoke a pipe.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:17.440
drink i got one i uh i don't think i've noticed you here before by the way are rumors true what

00:31:17.590 --> 00:31:22.970
rumors oh you know that the uh murderer oh there's nothing to worry about that's a very pretty girl

00:31:31.500 --> 00:31:32.280
I'm French.

00:31:32.930 --> 00:31:33.630
No, no.

00:31:33.950 --> 00:31:34.350
American.

00:31:34.490 --> 00:31:35.370
